`GetType` is already a short chain of branches, so there is little to gain. The rewrite keeps the same checks in the same order and adds a branch-prediction hint. The common case, an explicitly set `type`, becomes the fall-through path. The profile lookup is moved into a scoped local. Behavior is unchanged for every input.

```cpp
FIT_UINT8 Field::GetType() const
{
    const FIT_UINT8 t = type;
    if (__builtin_expect(t != FIT_UINT8_INVALID, 1))
        return t;

    const Profile::MESG* const p = profile;
    if ((p == NULL) || (profileIndex >= p->numFields))
        return FIT_UINT8_INVALID;

    return p->fields[profileIndex].type;
}
```